        "date": "2026-11-13T16:01:35Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(turning): a new Facing faces the stock allowance down to the part's top\n\nThe Facing seed took its heights from the mill fold: top = Top of\nModel and the facing plane = Bottom of Model (#214's part floor), so a\nFacing created by the MCP add_operation (seed_params) or the GUI\nquick-add laddered from the part's floor up to its top and cut the\npart away, leaving the stock allowance above it untouched. The seed\nnow states its own heights, like its stepdown: Top of Stock down to\nTop of Model.\n\nA part already at length (stock top == part top) makes that window\nlevel. The heights door called it an upward cut; a Facing, like a\nFace, now passes a level window there, and generate refuses it by\nname: \"nothing to face\".\n\nFixes #1409\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
